  message: "Resolved without code change: websocket_handler IS already mapped to WEBSOCKET_HANDLER entrypoint at packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/entrypoints.py:425-439 (since ADR-0003 v0.9.x). The `inert` status on docs/CONCEPTS.md was a false positive caused by generate-concepts' regex not detecting the `concept_type == \"X\"` and `concept_type in (\"X\", \"Y\")` consumer patterns. Filing a separate invariant item (INV-*) for the generate-concepts undercount bug — concepts including error_handler, websocket_handler, event_handler, middleware, command, liveview, graphql_resolver, and many more are already consumed via those patterns but show as inert. Fix will be an upgraded regex in scripts/generate-concepts, which will flip ~15-20 concepts inert → live in one PR."  # a104
